	abstract = {In India, the Small and Medium Enterprise (SME) sector is also facing the growing exposure to fraudulent practices as per this fact which is worsened by the complexity of regulation structures and limitation of auditors. In order to overcome this difficulty, we have designed a multi layered artificial intelligence platform that consolidates Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) to perform a full scale analysis of transactions, Variational Autoencoders (VAEs) to identify numerical anomalies, and IndicBERT, which process multilingual and textual data. An important component of our architecture is the brand new Regulatory Aware Contextual Fusion Module that is carefully constructed to ensure that it complies with the Financial Reporting Standards as introduced by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) XBRL schema and the reporting indeed required by the Goods and Services Tax (GST). Initial testing of validation showed that the performance of IndicBERT was impaired when presented with entries of the Tamil language, where a two step fine tuning program was required. The system also employs the Llama 3 language model for automated audit narratives while preserving data privacy. © 2026 IEEE.},
