	affiliations = {School of Electricals and Electronics, Sathyabama Institute of Science and Technology, Dept. of Ece, Tamil Nadu, Chennai, India; School of Science and Humanities, Sathyabama Institute of Science and Technology, Dept. of Cs, Tamil Nadu, Chennai, India; School of Computing, Sathyabama Institute of Science and Technology, Dept. of Cse, Tamil Nadu, Chennai, India},
	abstract = {India's Unified Payments Interface (UPI) has grown rapidly in popularity, increasing the risk of fraudulent transactions and necessitating efficient and interpretable detection systems. In this paper, an AI-powered system for real-time fraud detection and Anti-Money Laundering (AML) compliance in digital payments, FinGuard Pro, is presented. The solution incorporates a sanctions list screening module, a transaction screening module, a machine learning-based detection engine with post-hoc interpretability, and an easy-to-use dashboard for user engagement. Under the direction of domain knowledge, Reserve Bank of India (RBI) laws, and known fraud typologies, we developed a synthetic dataset that mimics real digital transaction patterns to overcome the absence of publicly available datasets and privacy issues. According to our experimental evaluation, FinGuard Pro detects 94% of fraudulent transactions with a precision level that is acceptable enough to reduce false positives. Scalable deployment, regulatory compliance, and thorough testing in a variety of fraud situations are all supported by the modular design. These findings demonstrate how the system might improve explainability, compliance, and fraud prevention in India's rapidly developing digital payment environment. © 2025 IEEE.},
