	abstract = {This research proposes a high-accuracy occupational crime detection framework for human resource systems by combining transformer-based behavioral NLP models with fairness-aware machine learning techniques. Using fine-tuned BERT embeddings and structured psychometric-demographic annotations, the model was evaluated across diverse HR contexts including access violations, grievance risk, fraud detection, and compliance breaches. It consistently achieved classification accuracies exceeding 94.7%, with F1-scores reaching 0.94 and fairness scores up to 0.93. Compared to baseline models, the enhanced framework reduced false positive rates by over 21% and improved interpretability through SHAP-based visualizations and feature-attribution maps. Integration of behavioral telemetry, contextual embeddings, and ethical scoring mechanisms enabled role-sensitive risk stratification, outperforming static rule-based compliance systems. Unlike resource-intensive ensemble pipelines, the proposed model maintained average training times under 1.8 seconds, ensuring deployment feasibility in large-scale enterprise HR platforms. The framework supports cross-functional scalability and is adaptable to varied policy environments without structural reconfiguration.  © 2025 IEEE.},
