	affiliations = {Amrita School of Computing, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham, Chennai, India},
	abstract = {Credit card fraud has become a fast-moving, complex threat that traditional detection systems have a hard time stopping. This paper takes a new approach by combining Explainable AI (XAI) with blockchain's unbreakable trust layer to make a fraud-detection system that is not only quick and accurate, but also clear and impossible to hack. Our solution makes each alert easier to understand for analysts and stakeholders by using a group of modern classifiers (XGBoost, LightGBM, and CatBoost) and adding clear and easy-to-understand explanations from SHAP and LIME. A lightweight smart-contract framework on Ethereum logs every flagged transaction and its explanation digest at the same time. This makes an unchangeable audit trail that regulators and auditors can trust which not only keeps fraud alerts safe and clear, but, also helps people follow the rules by keeping a permanent and verifiable record of detection decisions. Blockchain removes concerns about data tampering or manipulation, which are common problems with centralized fraud detection systems. This design is built into a real-time streaming pipeline and gives verdicts in less than a second. This allows banks and other financial institutions to respond quickly to new fraud schemes and limit their losses. The system's design uses modern stream processing tools to handle a lot of transactions quickly and accurately, without losing any of the information's meaning. In today's fast-paced digital economy, where fraudsters take advantage of every millisecond of delay in detection, this ability to respond quickly is very important. The resulting framework establishes a new benchmark for next-generation financial security systems by discouraging fraudulent activity and strengthening stakeholder confidence through indisputable evidence of integrity and explainability. © 2025 IEEE.},
