	abstract = {Accounting and finance are being fundamentally transformed by Artificial Intelligence (AI): intelligent automation, sophisticated analytics, and data-driven decisions can be achieved. Conventional financial systems, which have long relied on manual approaches and rule-based solutions, are undergoing more and more additions of Machine Learning, Deep Learning, Natural Language Processing, and Robotic Process Automation. The technologies are in support of automated bookkeeping, intelligent auditing, fraud detection, credit risk modeling, portfolio optimization, and financial forecasting. AI systems enhance efficiency, accuracy, and realtime generation of insights after analyzing large volumes of structured and unstructured financial data. The current review paper is a systematic study of recent advances in accounting and finance of AI use, where methods are divided into categories, and key practical applications are identified. It also examines the latest trends, such as explainable AI, financial reporting using generative AI, and systems that are powered by AI and support decision-making. In spite of major improvements, issues can still be encountered regarding the interpretability of the model, regulatory compliance, data privacy, ethical aspects, and the risk of cybersecurity. The paper proposes research gaps that are critical and maps the directions in the future to facilitate transparent, reliable, and scalable intelligent financial systems that add to the research in academia and industry practice.  © 2026 IEEE.},
