	affiliations = {SAP Solution Architect, Technology Hub Inc, Glen Allen, VA, United States},
	abstract = {The issue of financial integrity is also critical in the contemporary business since there is an increased risk in the regulatory investigations of organizations, more intricate compliance systems, and even increased fraud and misreporting. As companies adopt the use of SAP S/4HANA as an intelligent enterprise resource planning (ERP) system, companies are revising workflow models with a view to making them transparent, accountable, and regulatory compliant. Provided in this paper, the topic of artificial intelligence (AI) implementation in SAP S/4HANA operations is touched upon as a way of enhancing financial integrity and reducing risks along with facilitating regulatory compliance. Using a literature analysis on the topic, we are examining the ways in which the standard financial controls are being revolutionized by AI driven automation, detection of anomalies and predictive analytics. A methodology framework is provided to analyze the risk-sensitive processes of accounts payable, revenue recognition, audit trial management. The findings point to the possible advantages of AI-based SAP S/4HANA named the possibility to minimize manual error, increase fraud detection, and accuracy of compliance reporting. The discussion focuses on the proportion between technological opportunities and challenges, especially in the data governance, explanation of the meaning of AI decisions, and legality, and whether these changes and regulations are accepted. Although the process of AI integration has enormous potential advantage, effective drawbacks are high cost, organizational resistance to change, and the complexity of its association to new financial laws. Future studies should aim at creating explainable AI solutions, scalable governance frameworks and industry specific compliance templates which would be consistent across the global and local regulatory landscape. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.},
