	abstract = {Detecting financial fraud is hard because it involves data from many different sources, which makes collecting and processing it complicated. Most current systems rely on manually built ETL pipelines that often break and are hard to expand. In this work, we introduce FraudGuard AI, a web-based platform that can handle data without needing a fixed structure. The system uses Google's Gemini Large Language Model (LLM) to match columns from uploaded CSV files to a standard set of features, so there's no need for strict ETL rules and the system becomes more flexible. After this, a hybrid rule-based engine spots suspicious transactions. For each case it flags, LLM writes a short explanation to make it easier for analysts to understand. Tests show that this step adds only about 0.85 seconds per schema alignment. This is a small delay compared to how much better the system handles different types of data. Overall, FraudGuard AI provides a practical and transparent way to monitor financial activity automatically.  © 2026 IEEE.},
