	abstract = {The rate at which financial transactions and complexity in the market is rising in FinTech has led to the necessity of having accurate, adaptive and interpretable analytics systems. Conventional forecasting and fraud detection systems lack the ability to process multi-dimensional and non homogenous data and fluctuating market environments. The paper has introduced a metaheuristic-optimized deep neural network framework, which combines hybrid feature selection with the use of the Ant Lion Optimization (ALO) and the Grey Wolf Optimizer (GWO), attention-based deep learning with the use of the temporal and spatial pattern recognition, and the hybrid hyperparameter optimization with the use of the Ant Lion Optimization (ALO) and the Whale Optimization Algorithm (WOA). The framework is tested on historical stock and transaction data sets that obtained RMSE=1.62, R=0.94 in predicting and Accuracy = 95.4, F1 -score = 94.2 in the classification tasks. The importance of each of the modules is found in robustness analysis of anomalies in the market and ablation analysis. These findings indicate that the suggested framework offers precise, reliable, and interpretable financial analytics that offers a scalable solution to a number of FinTech applications and aids in strategic and data-driven decision-making in financial affairs. © 2026 IEEE.},
