	affiliations = {Department of Computer Science and Engineering (CS), SRM Madurai College for Engineering and Technology, Sivaganga, Pottapalayam, India; Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Vel Tech Rangarajan Dr.Sagunthala R&D, Institute of Science and Technology, Avadi, Chennai, India; Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Chennai Institution of Technology, Chennai, India; Department of Information Technology, Velammal College of Engineering and Technology, Madurai, India; Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Saveetha School of Engineering, Saveetha Institute of Medical and Technical Sciences, Chennai, India; Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, SCAD College of Engineering and Technology, Cheranmahadevi, India},
	abstract = {Ensuring food quality and safety across complex agricultural supply chains remains a global challenge. Traditional inspection and traceability systems rely on manual assessment and centralized databases, which are prone to human error, data manipulation, and limited scalability. To address these issues, this study proposes AgriTraceNet: A Deep Learning and Blockchain Synergy for Intelligent Food Quality Verification, an integrated framework that combines advanced artificial intelligence with decentralized ledger technology to achieve secure, explainable, and automated food quality assurance. The system employs a Swin Transformer for high-precision visual inspection of food products, identifying defects and surface degradations. DeepSVDD is utilized for unsupervised anomaly detection, capturing deviations from normal quality distributions, while a Temporal Convolutional Network (TCN) processes time-series sensor data to predict freshness and spoilage trends. A middleware data gateway connects these deep learning models to a Hyperledger Fabric blockchain and IPFS-based off-chain storage, ensuring tamper-proof provenance recording and efficient data access. Smart contracts (chaincode) automatically record model outputs and verification hashes, establishing immutable, auditable proof of product integrity. Additionally, Grad-CAM and other explainability techniques are integrated to enhance trust and interpretability of AI-driven decisions. The combination of IoT data signing, blockchain validation, and deep learning analytics ensures end-to-end transparency, security, and reliability. By fusing intelligent inspection with decentralized verification, AgriTraceNet provides a scalable and trustworthy framework for real-time food quality monitoring, reducing fraud, improving traceability, and strengthening consumer confidence in global food systems. © 2025 IEEE.},
