	abstract = {Phishing, insider exploitation, and sophisticated transaction manipulation are examples of the kind of cyberthreats that financial institutions must contend with. They are not by themselves. This is occurring as a result of the digitization of the financial sector. When using traditional cybersecurity methodologies, it can be challenging to identify new attack patterns that are considerably more complicated. Because of the complexity and continual nature of digital transactions, this is the case. The purpose of this research is to improve banking cybersecurity by utilizing artificial intelligence to identify insider threats, phishing efforts, and irregular financial activities in real time. For the purpose of providing a proactive and customizable risk reduction solution, the disclosed technique makes use of machine learning, natural language processing, and behavioral analytics. Three primary components make up the framework. To identify potential dangers within the organization, the first one employs analytics of user activity. Monitoring the frequency of logins, data access, and changes in work routines are all ways to accomplish this goal. By analyzing language and context clues, the second module is able to identify phishing attempts that are made in chat logs, emails, and other channels. This is accomplished through the utilization of natural language processing and deep learning models. The third phase involves the utilization of algorithms for the purpose of monitoring financial transactions and identifying abnormalities. The reason for this could be that the transaction is overly large, that it occurs frequently, or that it is sent to the incorrect individual. These elements come together to form a sophisticated security system that is able to adapt to new information and threats. Research demonstrated that the AI model can identify cyber hazards without false positives. Explainable AI components help security analysts comprehend model results and make decisions. Because they can evaluate data in real time, financial institutions can discover threats before breaches. This protects their money and reputation. This essay discusses how AI has profoundly altered financial system cybersecurity. Predictive analytics, linguistic intelligence, and behavioral profiling enable financial organizations prevent rather than defend. In a constantly evolving cyber environment, AI strengthens digital systems, creates customer trust, enforces regulations, and improves operations.  © 2025 IEEE.},
