	abstract = {In the age of digital payment ecosystems, financial management and transaction analysis for consumers has become more complex. Financial intelligence systems are mostly built for fraud detection or expenditure monitoring with minimal support with adaptive optimization for consumers. In this paper, an AI Driven Post Purchase Financial Intelligence Framework of intelligent consumer transaction optimization with behavioral learning and explainable financial analytics is proposed. The proposed framework is designed to combine Light GBM for expenditure prediction, LSTM for learning transaction sequences, adaptive recommendations generation as well as explainable AI mechanisms under a single framework. For the experimental evaluation publicly available financial transaction and e-commerce datasets were used. The framework was evaluated under different transactions by accuracy, F1 score, stability of recommendations and optimization efficiency metrics. Experimental results showed that the accuracy of transactions being predicted was 96.1% and stability of financial recommendations was higher than the existing financial analytics models. The proposed framework also showed a stable scalability and secure anomaly monitoring performance, suggesting its applicability in real time intelligent financial decision support systems in today's digital commerce landscape. © 2026 IEEE.},
