	abstract = {This research introduces a real-time behavioral anomaly and fraud detection architecture tailored for FinTech systems by integrating temporal deep learning with federated and explainable AI (XAI) pipelines. Utilizing LSTM Autoencoders, Graph Neural Networks (GNNs), and reinforcement-based feedback loops, the system was evaluated on over 220 million transactions from mobile wallets, algorithmic trading, and cross-border remittance platforms. The framework attained classification accuracy surpassing 97.85%, F1-scores of 0.947, and latency below 110 milliseconds per transaction stream. Compared to static threshold and non-temporal baselines, it reduced false positives by 41.3% and improved interpretability via SHAP, DeepLIFT, and counterfactual XAI layers. Behavioral embeddings, transaction graph profiling, and anomaly temporal vectors facilitated granular detection across adversarial and high-frequency patterns. Unlike traditional resource-intensive systems, model training remains under 1.9 seconds per adaptive window, supporting real-time retraining under concept drift. The architecture is modular, privacy-aware, and deployable across diverse FinTech infrastructures without retraining core layers.  © 2025 IEEE.},
