	abstract = {Financial ecosystems produce vast flows of heterogeneous, high-velocity transaction data in which anomalies such as fraud, jerky payments, and market manipulation - and the associated financial risk - are rampant. Conventional machine-learning methods tend to struggle with changing patterns, data imbalance, and the need for interpretability. In this paper, we propose HybridAgent-ML, a hybrid machine-learning framework for financial anomaly detection driven by an intelligent agent to acquire adaptive preprocessing, ensemble fusion, and explainable analysis. It employs autonomous agents that focus on data cleaning, imbalance correction, and drift monitoring and then uses a hybrid core that combines an autoencoder with gradient-boosted and random-forest classifiers. SHAP and LIME interpretive layers are used here to justify the decision. Using the publicly available Kaggle Credit Card Fraud Detection Dataset, we show that our method outperforms conventional baselines across Recall at any Precision, Balanced Precision, and Interpretability (i.e., the ability to understand the model). It provides a framework with a roadmap for scalable, trustworthy, and auditable anomaly detection in finance. © 2026 IEEE.},
