	year = {2025},
	journal = {2025 12th International Conference on Reliability, Infocom Technologies and Optimization ,Trends and Future Directions, ICRITO 2025},
	pages = {},
	doi = {10.1109/ICRITO66076.2025.11241223},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105029815264?origin=resultslist},
	affiliations = {Dronacharya College of Engineering, Deptarment of Cse, Gurugram, India; Manipal University Jaipur, Department of Computer Applications, Jaipur, India; Psit College of Higher Education, Department of Computer Applications, U.P, Kanpur, India; Amity Institute of Information Technology, Amity University Uttar Pradesh, Uttar Pradesh, 201313, India},
	abstract = {Spam messages remain a significant issue in online communication, tending to promote fraud and cyberbullying. Despite common email services supporting spam filters, they do not always make good judgments, occasionally mislabelling valid emails or failing to flag malicious ones. This research explores employing explainable machine learning models to enhance both the accuracy and transparency of spam filtering. Supervised machine learning algorithms such as Random Forest, Naïve Bayes, Support Vector Machine, Logistic Regression, and Decision Trees were experimented on a dataset of 5,574 messages of the UCI Machine Learning Repository. The Machine Learning (ML) algorithm, such as support vector machine, outperforms with an accuracy of 98.0% with a precision 96.14%, with a recall and F1-score of 97.18% and 0.96, respectively, while K-nearest neighbor performs less among all machine learning models. Besides this method, LIME is employed for explainability so that intuitions are obtained from the model's estimates, qualifying perceptions of why certain emails are labelled as spam. Its indicating that characters like 't', 'a', 'o', 'u', and 'g' are less likely to be labelled as spam. The character 'c' indicates that the mail should be labeled spam. The study concludes that integrating XAI not only improves the effectiveness of spam detection but also supports the interpretability of results, which is critical for user trust and further refinement of spam filtering mechanisms, particularly in identifying nuanced threats such as stock market-related spam.  © 2025 IEEE.},
