	abstract = {Online advertising platforms continue to face a challenge of click fraud which also leads to advertisers to bear needless expenses, thus reducing the advertisers to low returns on investment, and eventually loss of faith in the advertisement platforms. The majority of the current solutions merely attempt to identify the occurrence of click frauds after they have occurred, which offers minimal protection against advanced and high scale attacks using click fraud. The Proactive Click Fraud Prevention and Mitigation Framework (PCF-PM) presented in this paper does not conform to conventional detection-based remedies, but rather integrates real-time fraud intelligence, risk-based prevention strategies, and adaptive mitigation strategies. The proposed structure makes use of Hybrid Adaptive Ensemble of LightGBM, Recurrent Neural Networks as well as AutoEncoder based Anomaly Detection to offer comprehensive fraud intelligence. The system has preventive measures and damage control policies in a closed-loop system with the use of dynamic risk scoring and fraud behavior typing. Experimental analysis of actual clickstream data sets indicates that the PCF-PM framework is more effective than real-life machine learning and deep learning-based solutions in terms of higher detection rates, higher fraud block rates, large cost cuts to advertisers, and lower false positive rates. The results of the experiment confirm the effectiveness of proactive and adaptive defense strategies to protect online advertising system against advanced attack of click fraud. Moreover, the adaptive feedback control can be used to help the framework adapt to concept drift and adversarial evolution in fraud patterns. © 2026 IEEE.},
