	affiliations = {Netaji Subhas Univeristy of Technology, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, New Delh, India},
	abstract = {Identity document verification systems are increasingly susceptible to complicated presentation attacks (PAs) such as copy-move fraud and facial morphing. The current visual-based deep learning methods are highly unreliable and difficult for explanation. In this paper we present a transparent multistage framework to identify identity document fraud from structured metadata and document images side-by-side. The architecture combines an image encoder based on EfficientNet with a metadata encoder using BiLSTM, which is connected by deep feature fusion. It is fine-tuned via a 2 -step finetuning scheme. Experimental results on the synthesized dataset demonstrate that our approach achieves better performance in all types of attacks with standard PAD metrics. Grad-CAMs also contribute to transparency and forensic interpretability for tooltips. © 2026 IEEE.},
