	affiliations = {Mumbai, India; International Bank, MKSSS’s Cummins College of Engineering for Women, Pune, India},
	abstract = {Credit Cards have become an integral component of today’s digital age. For both personal and commercial transactions they offer speed, convenience and global accessibility. Despite the instantaneous characteristic of these transactions, each payment operation must be carefully analyzed to detect potentially fraudulent activities. Fraud detection involves evaluating multiple parameters like transaction amount, location, user behavior patterns and historical spending analysis, to identify patterns that may indicate unauthorized use. Selecting the most appropriate Machine Learning Model for this evaluation and explaining the results of that model is a tedious task. This study suggests a novel method that leverages advanced AI techniques, such as Agentic Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Explainable AI that can enhance the accuracy and transparency of fraud detection. Agentic AI enables smart decision-making by autonomously assessing complex transaction patterns, while Explainable AI provides interpretable insights into why certain transactions are flagged as suspicious. The aim of our credit card fraud detection system is to accurately identify and prevent fraudulent transactions in real-time by analyzing the patters in payment parameters. By integrating Agentic AI tools for intelligent decision making and Explainable AI for outcome reasoning, this system not only reduces financial loses but also builds a relation of trust with users and financial institutions. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.},
