	abstract = {Blockchain networks, though they are secure from a decentralization perspective, are still quite vulnerable to fraudulent activities such as money laundering, phishing, and hijacking of interconnected chains. The existing methods of fraud detection in research are disjointed and only consider limited datasets, single modeling paradigms, or isolated aspects of fraud detection. In this work, we talk about a new system that spots fraud and works well on all parts of the blockchain. It uses many types of machine learning, works in real-time, fights against attacks, and looks at data across different chains. Our system is built not just to find fraud, but it also uses graph neural networks to see how data relates, fights back against four kinds of attacks, and has a fast, real-time link. Our goal is to show a ready-to-use, safe, and fair AI system that makes big changes in how we find fraud in blockchain. It fills all the big gaps in research and helps with real use out there.  © 2025 IEEE.},
