	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105052907955?origin=resultslist},
	affiliations = {Department of Information Systems, DePaul University, Chicago, United States},
	abstract = {Claims Rejections due to Missing Codes, Incorrect Modifiers, Missing Billing Information, and Misaligned Documentation have remained a problem in the healthcare sector. These inefficiencies have a significant role in revenue loss, administrative burden and exposure to audit risks. To address these issues, this paper will introduce an AI-Powered Real-Time Claim Denial Blocker with Blockchain Audit, a hybrid intelligence scheme that integrates generative AI and blockchain technology to provide end-to-end transparency and accountability to healthcare claims processing. The system suggested consists of a GPT-based engine of fix suggestions to automatically detect, analyze, and suggest corrections to possible claim denials prior to submission. At the same time, Ethereum-based smart contract is guaranteed to log all transactions and modifications, making them fully traceable, resistant to data alterations, and compliant with regulations due to immutable audit trails. The model is built in Python, Web3.py, Solidity, and Power BI and combines the data preprocessing, anomaly detection, and blockchain verification steps into a smooth workflow to manage the intelligent claim management. Discussing the proposed hybrid design in relation to recent AI-Blockchain models, it is possible to note that the manual intervention decreases, the audit preparedness increases, and the efficiency of approval is improved. The results confirm that explainable AI used together with decentralized audit designs establishes a scalable base of transparent, fraud-free, and compliant digital healthcare ecosystems. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2027.},
