	abstract = {The banking sector faces challenges in loan approval due to inefficiency, inconsistent decision-making, and fraud risks. This paper proposes an AI-driven, cloud-enabled loan approval system that integrates a multi-task Siamese neural network (MTSNN) with the Lion (evolved sign momentum) optimizer for enhanced accuracy and stability. The MTSNN jointly performs loan approval prediction, credit scoring, and fraud detection using shared feature learning and task-specific heads, while Lion ensures noise-resilient and fast convergence. A hybrid cloud deployment (AWS + Outposts) ensures low-latency decision-making with compliance to KYC/AML regulations. Experiments on the RPubs Loan Approval dataset (614 instances; 80/20 split; stratified sampling) show superior performance: accuracy (97.94%), precision (98.15%), recall (92.98%), and F1-score (94.54%). Comparative analysis with interpretable models (Random Forest, XGBoost, LightGBM) and ablation studies confirm the advantages of MTSNN and Lion. Fairness evaluation (gender and income groups) and SHAP-based interpretability demonstrate transparent and unbiased decision-making. The proposed system reduces financial risks while enabling faster, secure, and explainable loan approvals. While demonstrated in banking, the proposed MTSNN + Lion + Cloud framework is generalizable to other decision-making applications such as insurance, healthcare eligibility, and e-commerce risk assessment. © The Author(s), under exclusive licence to Springer-Verlag GmbH Germany, part of Springer Nature 2026.},
