	affiliations = {Faculty of Information Technology, University of Science, Ho Chi Minh City, Viet Nam; Vietnam National University, Ho Chi Minh City, Viet Nam; FPT University, Ho Chi Minh City, Viet Nam},
	abstract = {Stock market fraud is characterized by complex temporal dynamics, causal interdependencies between firms, and severe data gaps due to delayed disclosures. Traditional anomaly detection methods are rendered ineffective under such conditions because of evolving normality, long-tail fraud types, and missing regulatory signals. A novel method called Causal GNN is introduced, which integrates causal graph construction from regulatory enforcement chains, self-supervised pre-training via masked reconstruction and contrastive learning, ImputeGAP for temporal gap imputation under Missing Not at Random (MNAR) missingness, and multi-level explainable AI using Shapley Additive exPlanations (SHAP), counterfactuals, and path tracing. The method is evaluated on a new dataset of 1,226 real-world fraud cases from Vietnam’s State Securities Commission (SSC) and Taiwan’s Financial Supervisory Commission (FSC), enriched with stock prices and filing delays up to September 2025. Causal GNN achieves 0.847 Area Under the Receiver Operating Characteristic Curve (AUROC) and up to 42% relative improvement over unsupervised baselines on zero-shot fraud types. The dataset, source code, and an intelligent interactive explainable AI dashboard are publicly released. The contributions address key challenges in motivation, related work, dataset construction, method design, experiments, and fraud type explanations. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd. 2026.},
