	abstract = {This study presents a hybrid neuro-symbolic framework for real-time banking fraud detection that integrates deep learning and symbolic reasoning techniques to capture the accuracy and interpretability of the model. And suggest a novel system which leverages Transformers as anomaly detectors on transaction data, whilst combining them with symbolic reasoning for logical explanations of the flagged records. These explanations are further processed by Large Language Models (LLMs) to generate human-readable descriptions that contribute to the transparency of risk attribution and build trust in the system. The hybrid models' performances were significantly better than the traditional classifiers, achieving a higher precision, recall and F1-score with lower false positive false negative rates. The clarity, relevance, and comprehensibility ratings of the LLM-augmented explanations were higher than those based on standard symbolic outputs, greatly enhancing analyst decision-making. It also showed good real-time performance, with a throughput of 10,000 transactions per minute and low latency that would be amenable to deployment in production banking systems. Ryan's results emphasize the powerful combination of deep learning with symbolic reasoning for fraud mitigation and explainability while providing a credible option to inhibit banking interceptions. In future work, and plan to scale up this approach for use in realistic systems and improve the quality of explanations further. © 2026 IEEE.},
