	abstract = {With advancements in big data analytics and artificial intelligence, the banking sector is witnessing rapid changes which bring both opportunities and hurdles in understanding customer behaviour. We propose a securityaware explainable AI (XAI)-patterned prediction framework for banking customers behaviour prediction, which is equipped with the capability to conduct accurate predictive analysis such as forecasting/fraud detection, pattern mining and anomaly detection. To recognize complex non-linear customer behavioural patterns, a hybrid approach combining XGBoost, Cat Boost, LightGBM and a Voting Classifier is used. The framework is evaluated via a synthetic case study with consolidated and graphical outcomes, including SHAPempowered element credits and hazard-driven irregularity scores. The Voting Classifier, XGBoost, Cat Boost and LightGBM achieved high prediction accuracies of 0.95,0.93, 0.92 and 0.94 respectively. Furthermore, the integrated anomaly module successfully identified high-risk outliers, indicating strong fraud detection efficacy with anomaly score > 0.8. This method, with enhanced security, outperforms the traditional unbalanced classification methods by AUPRC, recall, F1-score. Moreover, the in-built anomaly module successfully captured high risk outliers (anomaly scores > 0.8), thus assisting in fraud detection capabilities. This method is more efficient in all AUPRC, recall, F1-score, G-mean over traditional unbalanced classification methods with security computerization. These results also demonstrate great generalizability in banking datasets, making it a safe.  © 2025 IEEE.},
